{"id":"task-003","title":"Foundation: types, config, state, and helper modules","description":"Create the foundation layer for multi-model routing (issue #86). Work on branch `feature/86-multi-model-routing`.\n\n## Steps\n\n### 0. Create feature branch\n```bash\ngit checkout -b feature/86-multi-model-routing\n```\n\n### 1. Read the analysis and existing code\nRead `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/issue-86-analysis.md` for full context.\nRead existing code: `lib/semblr-config.ts`, `lib/state.ts`, `src/semblr.ts` to understand conventions.\n\n### 2. Add types\nIn a new section in `lib/semblr-config.ts` (or a new file if that's cleaner), define:\n```typescript\n// Phase names the LLM can self-report\ntype PhaseName = \"thinking\" | \"executing\" | \"stuck\" | \"reporting\" | \"reviewing\" | \"verifying\";\n\n// Map from phase to model ID (null = stay on current model)\ntype PhaseModelMap = Record<PhaseName, string | null>;\n\n// Config for multi-model routing\ninterface MultiModelRoutingConfig {\n  enabled: boolean;        // opt-in, default false\n  maxSwitches: number;     // switch limit per cycle\n  phaseModelMap: PhaseModelMap;\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Add config toggle to `lib/semblr-config.ts`\nAdd `multiModelRouting` to the SemblrConfig interface:\n- `enabled`: boolean, default `false` (opt-in)\n- `maxSwitches`: number, default `3`\n- `phaseModelMap`: PhaseModelMap with the Ollama-Cloud hardcoded map\n\n### 4. Add state fields to `lib/state.ts`\nAdd to the conversation state:\n- `switchCounter: number` (tracks switches per cycle, resets each cycle)\n- `currentPhase: PhaseName | null` (current reported phase)\n- `pendingModelSwitch: string | null` (model to switch to at agent_end)\n\n### 5. Create `lib/resolve-model-id.ts` (NEW FILE)\n```typescript\n// Resolves Ollama-Cloud model IDs like \"glm-5.2:cloud\" to actual provider model IDs\n// For MVP: strip \":cloud\" suffix, keep the base name for ollama provider\nexport function resolveModelId(modelId: string): { provider: string; model: string };\n```\n- If modelId contains \":cloud\", strip it and use \"ollama\" provider\n- Otherwise, pass through as-is\n- Write unit tests alongside\n\n### 6. Create `lib/phase-model-map.ts` (NEW FILE)\nExport the hardcoded MVP phase→model map (from comment #2 on the issue):\n```typescript\nexport const MVP_PHASE_MODEL_MAP: PhaseModelMap = {\n  thinking: null,           // stay on default model for thinking\n  executing: \"glm-5.2:cloud\",\n  stuck: \"kimi-k2.6:cloud\",\n  reporting: \"gemma4:12b:cloud\",\n  reviewing: \"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud\",  \n  verifying: \"deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\",\n};\n```\nAlso export a function `getModelForPhase(phase: PhaseName, map: PhaseModelMap): string | null`.\n\n### 7. Write unit tests\nFor `resolveModelId` and `getModelForPhase`. Follow existing test patterns.\n\n### 8. Verify\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit   # typecheck\nnpx vitest run     # run tests\n```\n\nWrite all findings/decisions to `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-003-output.md`.\nDo NOT rely on stdout — write all results to files.","status":"complete","agent_id":"coder","dependencies":[],"files_touched":["lib/semblr-config.ts","lib/state.ts","lib/resolve-model-id.ts","lib/phase-model-map.ts"],"execution_order":3,"created":"2026-06-24T08:37:23.089Z"}
{"id":"task-004","title":"Extension: tool registration, handler, model switching, announcements","description":"Implement the core multi-model routing feature in the Semblr extension. You are continuing from task-003 (Foundation). Make sure you're on branch `feature/86-multi-model-routing`.\n\n## Context\nRead `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/issue-86-analysis.md` and `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-003-output.md`.\nRead existing `src/semblr.ts` to understand tool registration pattern, agent_end handling, etc.\n\n**Uses inheritance** because you need all the type definitions, config, and state changes from task-003 loaded in session for accurate integration.\n\n## Steps\n\n### 1. Register `semblr_report_phase` tool\nIn `src/semblr.ts`, register a new native tool using the existing pattern (TypeBox schema):\n\n```typescript\n// Tool schema\nconst ReportPhaseSchema = Type.Object({\n  phase: Type.Union([\n    Type.Literal(\"thinking\"),\n    Type.Literal(\"executing\"),\n    Type.Literal(\"stuck\"),\n    Type.Literal(\"reporting\"),\n    Type.Literal(\"reviewing\"),\n    Type.Literal(\"verifying\"),\n  ]),\n});\n\n// Tool definition\n{\n  name: \"semblr_report_phase\",\n  description: \"Report your current generation phase to enable multi-model routing...\",\n  inputSchema: ReportPhaseSchema,\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Implement tool handler\nWhen the LLM calls `semblr_report_phase`:\n- Validate the phase value\n- Update `state.currentPhase`\n- Look up the target model from `phaseModelMap`\n- If target differs from current model AND switchCounter < maxSwitches → set `state.pendingModelSwitch`\n- Increment `switchCounter`\n- Return acknowledgment to the LLM (don't expose internal state)\n\n### 3. Implement model switching at agent_end\nIn the agent_end/new-turn boundary:\n- Check `state.pendingModelSwitch`\n- If set: switch to the pending model for the next turn\n- Reset `state.pendingModelSwitch`\n- DO NOT switch mid-generation — only at turn boundaries\n\n### 4. Stream announcements\nWhen a model switch occurs, emit a notice via pi's output stream:\n```\n[Multi-model] Switching to glm-5.2:cloud for executing phase (switch 1/3)\n```\n\n### 5. Context injection\nIn `lib/context-format.ts` and `lib/context-messages.ts`:\n- When `multiModelRouting.enabled` is true, inject the `semblr_report_phase` tool into the system prompt/tool list\n- The tool description should guide the LLM on when to report each phase\n- Follow existing tool injection patterns\n\n### 6. Guard rails\n- Feature is opt-in: only active when config.multiModelRouting.enabled === true\n- Respect maxSwitches limit (default 3)\n- If phase maps to null, stay on current model (no switch)\n- Never switch mid-generation\n- Idempotent: same phase reported twice should not double-count\n\n### 7. Verify\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit\nnpx vitest run\n```\n\nWrite all findings to `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-004-output.md`.","status":"failed","agent_id":"coder","dependencies":["task-003"],"files_touched":["src/semblr.ts","lib/context-format.ts","lib/context-messages.ts"],"execution_order":4,"created":"2026-06-24T08:37:37.692Z","continuesFrom":{"taskId":"task-003"}}
{"id":"task-005","title":"Behavior tests for multi-model routing","description":"Write comprehensive behavior tests for the multi-model routing feature (issue #86). Tests must be derived from the specification, NOT from implementation code.\n\n## Context\nRead `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/issue-86-analysis.md` for the full specification.\nRead task-003's output at `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-003-output.md` for type definitions and helper signatures.\nYou are working on branch `feature/86-multi-model-routing`.\n\n## Test Categories\n\n### 1. `resolveModelId` (lib/resolve-model-id.ts)\n- `\"glm-5.2:cloud\"` → `{ provider: \"ollama\", model: \"glm-5.2\" }`\n- `\"kimi-k2.6:cloud\"` → `{ provider: \"ollama\", model: \"kimi-k2.6\" }`\n- `\"openai/gpt-4\"` → `{ provider: \"openai\", model: \"gpt-4\" }` (no :cloud, pass through)\n- Edge: empty string, `\":cloud\"`, multiple `:cloud:cloud`\n\n### 2. `getModelForPhase` / phase map (lib/phase-model-map.ts)\n- Each phase maps to correct model (or null for thinking)\n- Unknown phase → returns null or throws\n- Map is immutable\n\n### 3. Tool schema validation\n- Valid phases (\"thinking\", \"executing\", \"stuck\", \"reporting\", \"reviewing\", \"verifying\") pass\n- Invalid phases (\"planning\", \"\", null) fail validation\n- Missing phase field fails validation\n\n### 4. Switch counter behavior\n- Tool call increments counter up to maxSwitches\n- After maxSwitches reached, further phase reports don't trigger switches\n- Counter resets at cycle boundaries (testable via state inspection)\n\n### 5. Model switching logic\n- Phase → null → stays on current model (no switch)\n- Phase → same model → no switch counted\n- Phase → different model → pending switch queued\n- Switch only applied at agent_end, not mid-generation\n\n### 6. Config gating\n- When disabled: tool calls are no-ops, no switches occur\n- When enabled: full routing active\n- Config defaults: enabled=false, maxSwitches=3\n\n### 7. Integration scenario\n- Full cycle: thinking→executing→stuck→reporting→verifying\n- Verify correct model transitions at each agent_end boundary\n\n## Requirements\n- Use vitest (matches project)\n- Follow existing test patterns in the project\n- Tests MUST pass against the implementation from task-003 and task-004\n- Write tests to files in `tests/` directory\n- Do NOT rely on stdout — write results to `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-005-output.md`\n\n## Verification\n```bash\nnpx vitest run\n```","status":"failed","agent_id":"tester","dependencies":["task-003"],"files_touched":["tests/"],"execution_order":5,"created":"2026-06-24T08:37:50.362Z"}
{"id":"task-006","title":"Integration, review, and acceptance verification","description":"Review and integrate the multi-model routing implementation (issue #86). All implementation tasks are complete; you are the final gate.\n\n## Context\nRead all prior outputs:\n- `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/issue-86-analysis.md` — the spec\n- `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-003-output.md` — foundation implementation\n- `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-004-output.md` — extension implementation\n- `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-005-output.md` — test results\n\nWork on branch `feature/86-multi-model-routing`.\n\n## Steps\n\n### 1. Verify branch and code\n```bash\ngit branch --show-current   # must be feature/86-multi-model-routing\ngit status                  # check for uncommitted changes\n```\n\n### 2. Run the test suite\n```bash\nnpx vitest run --coverage\n```\n- All tests must pass\n- Coverage must meet project threshold (80%)\n\n### 3. Run typecheck + lint\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit\nnpx biome check .\n```\n\n### 4. Review against acceptance criteria\nFrom the issue spec:\n- [ ] `semblr_report_phase` tool registered with correct TypeBox schema\n- [ ] Tool captures phase and updates state\n- [ ] Model switching happens only at agent_end boundaries\n- [ ] Switch counter enforced (maxSwitches limit)\n- [ ] Config opt-in (disabled by default)\n- [ ] Stream announcements on model switch\n- [ ] Null phase → stay on current model\n- [ ] Hardcoded MVP_PHASE_MODEL_MAP matches comment #2 (Ollama-Cloud)\n- [ ] resolveModelId correctly strips \":cloud\"\n\n### 5. Code quality review\n- [ ] Follows existing patterns in the codebase\n- [ ] Proper TypeScript types (no `any`)\n- [ ] Error handling for edge cases\n- [ ] No dead code or commented-out blocks\n- [ ] Imports are clean and minimal\n\n### 6. Fix issues or report\n- If minor issues: fix them directly\n- If major issues: report in output, do NOT silently pass\n\n### 7. Final verification\n```bash\nnpm run verify   # typecheck + lint + knip + test:coverage\n```\n\nWrite full review findings to `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-006-output.md`.\n\nStatus: DONE if all criteria pass. BLOCKED if major issues found.","status":"approved","agent_id":"reviewer","dependencies":["task-004","task-005"],"files_touched":[],"execution_order":6,"created":"2026-06-24T08:38:02.238Z"}
